---
code: K0001
title: Unexpected Token
description: "Encountered a token that is invalid in the current grammatical position"
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
tags: [parse, syntax, token]
deprecated: False
---

The parser encountered a token that cannot legally appear at the current position in the grammar—for example, a missing separator, a stray delimiter, or an operator where a type or expression was expected.

## Example

```kura
fn add(a: Int b: Int): Int => a + b
```

Provide the expected syntax token (such as a [`,`]{.expected} between parameters, a [`:`]{.expected} before a type annotation, or a matching closing delimiter):

```kura
fn add(a: Int, b: Int): Int => a + b
```

::: note
See the [EBNF](https://s0cks.github.io/kura) for the complete Kura grammar specification.
:::
